    "scenesThatPass": [
      "SUSAN: Good afternoon, Frederica.\nFREDERICA: Good afternoon, Mother.\nSUSAN: Excuse me. It's as I feared -- I must go to my daughter.",
      "SUSAN: Enchanté. Please forgive this intrusion but now that I'm fixed in town I can't rest with Frederica away.\nCATHERINE: Isn’t such anxiety new?\nSUSAN: Yes, it is -- I entirely agree. But now I’m in London where the instruction Frederica needs can so readily be found. Her voice has some prom…",
      "SUSAN: Frederica! You’re so kind to visit: Frederica will be delighted. How are the children -- especially my dear Frederick?\nCATHERINE: Very well, thank you--\nSUSAN: Frederica, come see who’s here! I can't express my gratitude for the hospitality you’ve extended us.",
      "CATHERINE: She’s greatly missed, by the little ones especially--\nSUSAN: What a moving sentiment of cousinly regard. My concern, my obligation, is to see the defects in Frederica’s education repaired.",
      "SUSAN: Might I confess something? Frederica and I have become such great friends it would be hard for me to part with her. You might have noticed t…\nSUSAN: Excuse me, are you quite well?\nCATHERINE: Sorry -- we'd so set our hearts on Frederica’s return.\nSUSAN: I understand completely. She's become an agreeable companion -- even her tendency to extreme quiet I’ve grown to find rather soothing. But t…"
    ]
  },
